cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its results, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "nids-protocol-benchmark: a controlled benchmark for evaluation-protocol effects in flow-based NIDS"
abstract: >-
  Code, configuration, seeds and the full 360-run results table for the
  controlled experiment accompanying the systematic survey "Deep Learning for
  Flow-Based Network Intrusion Detection (2022-2026)". The benchmark crosses
  three evaluation-protocol factors (train/test split, identity features, task)
  with five model families over eight standardised NetFlow corpora, holding data,
  preprocessing, seed and hyper-parameters constant so that differences are
  attributable to the protocol rather than the architecture.
